# Template for llm-server.sh's --api-key-file.
#
# This file is an example only - it is safe to commit to git. The real
# file must live OUTSIDE this repo, at:
#
#   ~/.config/llama-server/api-keys
#
# Format: llama-server's own --api-key-file format, not a shell script -
# one key per line, lines starting with # are comments. Despite this
# repo's single-user setup normally only needing one, the file (and
# llama-server's --api-key-file flag) supports multiple keys - one per
# line - if you ever want more than one valid credential (e.g. a separate
# key per client), hence the plural filename.
#
# This file is passed straight through to llama-server as a path
# (--api-key-file PATH), so key values themselves never become a CLI
# argument or a process environment variable - only readable by opening
# the file, same as any other 600-permissioned secret.
#
# Setup:
#   mkdir -p ~/.config/llama-server
#   chmod 700 ~/.config/llama-server
#   cp config/api-keys.example ~/.config/llama-server/api-keys
#   chmod 600 ~/.config/llama-server/api-keys
#   $EDITOR ~/.config/llama-server/api-keys

change-me
